From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:24:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Live module bindings and cycle-safe module Debug

1. Live module bindings: an export of a pre-bundled chunk can be
   undefined until its __esm init runs, so make_live_binding stores a
   null-proto marker carrying the host namespace handle and export
   name. Name reads (GetName, GetNameGlobal's declarative branch,
   GetNameAndLocator, GetNameOrUndefined) and module-namespace
   [[Get]]/try_get route through resolve_live_if_marker, which re-reads
   the live value through a host hook and caches it on the marker once
   defined. Markers are only stored as module exports, so name reads
   probe only when the binding lives in a module environment.
2. Non-recursive Debug for Module and IndirectBinding, so cyclic ES
   imports (A imports B imports A) don't overflow the stack in the
   derived formatter.
